| **G2.1 – Navigate to Storage**                    | The robot moves from its current location to the designated storage location where resources are available.                      | `-`              | Perform       | –                                           | AND          | Necessary action for the collection phase.                                                        |                    |                    |                    |
| **G2.2 – Request Resource**                       | The robot sends a message to the storage specifying the requested resources and waits for confirmation.                          | `-`              | Perform       | –                                           | AND          | Required to initiate resource retrieval.                                                          |                    |                    |                    |
| **G2.3 – Wait for Retrieval**                     | The robot remains at the storage until the resources are physically retrieved and ready for pickup.                              | `-`              | Perform       | –                                           | AND          | Must wait for retrieval to proceed.                                                               |                    |                    |                    |
| **G2.4 – Check Battery Level**                    | The robot queries its current battery level to determine if it is below the 10 % threshold.                                      | `-`              | Query         | Battery level                               | AND          | Battery check is necessary to decide whether to recharge.                                         |                    |                    |                    |
| **G2.5 – Recharge**                               | The robot travels to the recharging station to replenish its battery.                                                            | `-`              | Perform       | –                                           | AND          | Required when battery is low during collection.                                                   |                    |                    |                    |
| **G2.6 – Assign Mission to Another Robot**        | The robot informs the coordination system to reassign the remaining collection task to another robot.                            | `-`              | Perform       | –                                           | AND          | Ensures continuity of the mission when the original robot cannot continue.                        |                    |                    |                    |
| **G2.7 – Parallelize Collection Tasks**           | The system assigns multiple robots to different storages to collect resources concurrently.                                      | `#` (parallel)   | Perform       | –                                           | AND          | Parallel collection reduces overall mission time when multiple items are needed.                  |                    |                    |                    |
| **G3 – Execute Delivery Phase**                   | The robot carries the collected resources to the specified destination, handling battery constraints and potential failures.     | `;`              | Perform       | –                                           | AND          | All delivery steps must be executed in order to successfully deliver resources.                   |                    |                    |                    |
